<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
    Push Notifications entitlement. Without this, APNs registration
    fails with the error "未找到应用程序的 aps-environment 的授权字符串".

    v1.3.3 removed it while the server had no APNs key configured;
    restored once the server side (APNS_KEY_PATH / APNS_KEY_ID /
    APNS_TEAM_ID / APNS_BUNDLE_ID) and the privacy wording caught up.
    The App ID must also have "Push Notifications" ticked at
    developer.apple.com → Identifiers, and Info.plist declares
    UIBackgroundModes = remote-notification — the three move together.

    "development" is the value Xcode's capability toggle writes and
    what this file carried before the v1.3.3 removal: it works for
    Xcode debug builds (real device or iOS 16+ simulator on Apple
    Silicon) and ad-hoc / TestFlight builds. For App Store submission
    the shipped binary's entitlement comes from the distribution
    provisioning profile ("production"), so no separate Release-only
    entitlements file is needed.

    The app uses silent (content-available) pushes only — no alert /
    badge / sound permission required from the user at runtime.

    The App Sandbox + capability keys below are REQUIRED for the Mac
    Catalyst variant (v1.4.0+). iOS ignores them — the iOS sandbox is
    managed separately. Adding them here keeps a single entitlements
    file across both platforms.
    -->
    <key>aps-environment</key>
    <string>development</string>
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- HTTP/HTTPS calls to the user's ByWave server. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- EventKit mirror — read/write the user's local calendars. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- AVFoundation QR scanner — camera access on Catalyst. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.camera</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
